1
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:12,850
10 dollars shared between 8 friends is exactly 1.25 dollars each.

2
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:17,260
But 10 dollars shared between 6 is 1.666 and so on.

3
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:20,400
The calculator never finishes.

4
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:26,510
Why does 10 divided by 6 recur: because 6 has a factor 3, or because 6 is even?

5
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:30,000
Pause the video and choose.

6
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:32,430
Because 6 has a factor of 3.

7
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:36,420
8 is 2 times 2 times 2, so it fits into 1,000.

8
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:39,750
But no power of 10 divides by 3.

9
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:42,690
Remember: a fraction is a division.

10
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:46,940
3 eighths is 3 divided by 8, which is 0.375.

11
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:49,830
Write the fraction in its simplest form.

12
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:55,460
If the denominator's prime factors are only 2s and 5s, the decimal terminates.

13
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:57,530
Otherwise, it recurs.

14
00:00:57,580 --> 00:00:58,240
Your turn.

15
00:00:58,290 --> 00:01:00,810
Does 1 fortieth terminate, or recur?

16
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:04,130
Pause the video and choose.

17
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:07,200
40 is 2 times 2 times 2 times 5.

18
00:01:07,250 --> 00:01:10,370
Only 2s and 5s, so it terminates.

19
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:12,830
1 fortieth is 0.025.

20
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:16,920
To turn a recurring decimal into a fraction, call it X.

21
00:01:16,970 --> 00:01:19,670
If one digit repeats, multiply by 10.

22
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:23,050
If two digits repeat, multiply by 100.

23
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:27,490
Then subtract, so the repeating part cancels, and solve.

24
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:28,870
Here is the method.

25
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:31,390
Step 1: call the decimal X.

26
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:37,870
Step 2: multiply by 10, 100 or 1,000, to line up the repeats.

27
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:41,030
Step 3: subtract, then solve for X.

28
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:44,780
Step 4: simplify, and check on a calculator.

29
00:01:44,830 --> 00:01:47,840
Write 0.7 recurring as a fraction.

30
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:49,730
X is 0.777 and so on.

31
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,890
10 X is 7.777 and so on.

32
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:55,770
Subtract: 9 X is 7, so X is 7 ninths.

33
00:01:55,820 --> 00:01:59,530
Write 0.3 6, recurring, as a fraction.

34
00:01:59,580 --> 00:02:01,210
100 X is 36.3636.

35
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,480
Subtract X: 99 X is 36.

36
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:08,080
So X is 36 over 99, which is 4 elevenths.

37
00:02:08,130 --> 00:02:08,890
Your turn.

38
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:15,050
Write 0.4 5 recurring, 0.4545 and so on, as a fraction in its simplest form.

39
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:18,230
Pause and work it out.

40
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:20,730
100 X minus X: 99 X is 45.

41
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:25,980
X is 45 over 99, which simplifies to 5 elevenths.

42
00:02:26,030 --> 00:02:28,320
Does 21 over 56 terminate?

43
00:02:28,370 --> 00:02:31,200
Simplify first: it is 3 eighths.

44
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:33,090
8 is only 2s, so yes.

45
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:34,720
It is 0.375.

46
00:02:34,770 --> 00:02:38,010
Does 6 fifteenths give a terminating decimal?

47
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:38,960
Lucy answers.

48
00:02:39,010 --> 00:02:40,970
Which line is wrong?

49
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,170
Line 1 is wrong.

50
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:44,740
She did not simplify first.

51
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:47,900
6 fifteenths is 2 fifths, which is 0.4.

52
00:02:47,950 --> 00:02:49,590
It terminates.

53
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,100
Computers store numbers in base 2.

54
00:02:52,150 --> 00:02:56,380
Even 0.1 recurs in base 2, so tiny rounding errors appear.

55
00:02:56,430 --> 00:02:59,880
Banks use special methods to avoid them.

56
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:01,170
One last question.

57
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,670
Does 1 twelfth recur, or terminate?

58
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:07,010
Pause the video and choose.

59
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:09,270
12 is 2 times 2 times 3.

60
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:14,910
It has a factor of 3, so it recurs: 0.08333 and so on.

61
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,570
To remember: simplify first.

62
00:03:17,620 --> 00:03:21,210
Only 2s and 5s in the denominator: it terminates.

63
00:03:21,260 --> 00:03:23,250
Otherwise it recurs.

64
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:27,290
For recurring decimals: multiply, subtract, solve.

65
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:29,760
Check with a calculator.

66
00:03:29,810 --> 00:03:34,990
Great work! Now practise lesson 8.1 on Camday.
